ct sheet lists the added cells at (11,5), (11,7), (12,2) and so on. Each one is a top-panel cell shifted down by 10, which is one panel height plus the divider.\n- Pair 2: the pattern sits in the bottom-left panel. In the output it is copied unchanged into the top-left, top-right and bottom-right panels. For example, (11,5)=7 shows up at (1,5), (1,15) and (11,15).\n\nNothing is recoloured, mirrored or moved inside a panel. It is a plain copy, so the rule is:\n\n> Split the grid into panels using the divider lines. Find the panel that contains non-background cells, then paste that panel into every other panel at the same relative position.\n\n**Test input.** The pattern (3s, 2s and 6s) is in the top-middle panel, columns 10–18 and rows 0–8. It gets copied into the other five panels: top-left, top-right, and all three bottom panels. The dividers stay as they are.\n\n**Construction stages.** The student starts from the input. Each empty panel is filled with the copied pattern as one stage, followed by a final emit of the finished grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    boxes = panels(g)\n    # the source panel is the one holding the most non-background cells\n    def count(b):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = b\n        return int((g[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1] != bg).sum())\n    src = max(boxes, key=count)\n    sy0, sx0, sy1, sx1 = src\n    pattern = g[sy0:sy1+1, sx0:sx1+1].copy()\n    h, w = pattern.shape\n    out = g.copy()\n    for b in boxes:\n        if b == src:\n            continue\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = b\n        if (y1 - y0 + 1, x1 - x0 + 1) != (h, w):\n            continue\n        out[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1] = pattern\n        emit(out, f\"Copy the pattern from the source panel at rows {sy0}-{sy1}, cols {sx0}-{sx1} into the empty panel at rows {y0}-{y1}, cols {x0}-{x1}.\")\n    emit(out, \"Every panel now holds the same pattern; the divider lines are unchanged.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What the grid is made of.** Every grid is cut by full lines of colour 4 into equal 9×9 panels."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Pair 1 has one horizontal divider, so it has 2 panels."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Pair 2 has a horizontal and a vertical divider, so it has 4 panels."}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Nothing is recoloured, mirrored or moved inside a panel."}],"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Nothing is recoloured, mirrored or moved inside a panel."}],"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each one is a top-panel cell shifted down by 10, which is one panel height plus the divider."}],"boolean":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What changes.** In each input exactly one panel holds a pattern of coloured cells, and every other panel is empty."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"29e9d5804640a1f9706bee84ea6cb5a1b6df6cf4b5f2b01a31d902df6733366e","task_sha256":"8a6c06fb4843f3453f4e9aaf9a2b3960be8d892c2b21eef1eaeb526df972f83e","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
